{
  "dom_id": "step-q51497",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "What is the root of the function $g(x)=\\frac{x}{2}+4?$",
  "worked_solution": "The roots are the solutions to the equation $g(x)=0,$ which we solve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =-4 \\\\ x & =2(-4) \\\\ x & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has the single root $x=-8.$",
